      <TableCell>clusterIP is the service IP through which this DNS is made available. In the case of the default DNS, this will be a well known IP that is used as the default nameserver for pods that are using the default ClusterFirst DNS policy. In general, this IP can be specified in a pod’s spec.dnsConfig.nameservers list or used explicitly when performing name resolution from within the cluster. Example: dig foo.com @&lt;service IP&gt; More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/services-networking/service/#virtual-ips-and-service-proxies</TableCell>
